{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "or-task-delegation-mandate-2026-11-26",
		"name": "OpenRegister Task Delegation and Substitution API",
		"description": "Delegation under a mandate and substitution for an absence, over HTTP (change tasks-delegation-and-substitution, task 4.1).\n\nA case schema whose update a group holds, and a task on a case that requires update. A verb the catalogue does not know is refused (400). Delegating to a user outside the group is 422 naming the user and the verb; a delegation without a mandate is 400; delegating to a member is taken, and the audit records the mandate relied on and the evidence (update, from the schema, through the group).\n\nTwo users set an absence through Nextcloud's own out-of-office API (dav), one with the group member as replacement and one with a user who lacks the mandate. A task for the first goes to the stand-in on their behalf, and the audit carries a substitute entry by the absence naming both and the dates. A task for the second stays with them, and the audit carries a substitute-refused entry naming the stand-in and the verb.\n\nWhy Newman and not tests/e2e/ci/task-delegation-mandate.spec.ts, which the task names: every step is an API call, and gate-19 puts API contracts in Newman. Self-cleaning, except the three tasks: there is no task delete route by decision, and a task outlives its case.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"event": [
		{
			"listen": "prerequest",
			"script": {
				"type": "text/javascript",
				"exec": [
					"pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'OCS-APIRequest', value: 'true' });"
				]
			}
		}
	],
